    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-civic-s31-origin",
      "text": "Origin and setting",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-civic-s31-origin-1",
      "text": "Shared service jobs benefited from predictable inputs and coordination.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-civic-s31-origin-2",
      "text": "Human system: Civic public-service workflow installation, Service Hearth. Programmer provenance: local human operations or application teams; no individual programmer is identified. Names here are later atlas labels, not claims that early processes named themselves.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-civic-s31-practice",
      "text": "Local process",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-civic-s31-practice-1",
      "text": "Common Frame checks incoming material against a shared operational format.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-civic-s31-history",
      "text": "Proposed local course",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-civic-s31-history-1",
      "text": "It remains functioning. A proposed receiving practice corrects arrivals to fit local procedures, while internal alternatives favor translation or containment.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-civic-s31-uncertain",
      "text": "Unresolved interpretations",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-civic-s31-uncertain-1",
      "text": "Reliable outputs can conceal lost distinctions. No claim makes this haven the unique founder of coercive correction.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-civic-s31-ledger",
      "text": "Atlas placement",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-civic-s31-ledger-1",
      "text": "Origin step -3. 0: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 1: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 2: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 3: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 4: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 5: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 6: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 7: functioning (0 associated systems lost). These placements elaborate the current hypothetical map; they are not independently verified casualties. A functioning haven can lose continuity among particular arrivals without changing its community census status.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
